The first thing any program in this project does is read this directory.

Right now there is nothing to configure, because nothing has been built. When
there is, this is where the match parameters live: the seed, the map's shape
parameters, the team size, which commanders each player brought, and which
catalogue tables to load.

The reason this is a directory of files rather than a wall of command-line flags:
a match is a small number of decisions made before it starts, and they should be
readable, diffable, and copyable. A replay header is nearly the same set of
fields. Anything you would want to pin down and hand to somebody else so they can
run the same match belongs here.

What goes here eventually:
    seed              -- the match seed, one integer
    map               -- field size, lane spacing, connector length
    teams             -- how many players per side
    commanders        -- one line per player
    catalogues        -- which upgrade, boon, and unit tables to load
